## THE GOLDEN RULE

> **Make the impossible possible. Build the digital twin in 24 hours.**

This is the single unchangeable core goal for the next 24 hours. Every decision —
scope, shortcuts, what to fake, what to skip — gets measured against it. When in
doubt: **a working end-to-end simulation beats a beautiful half-finished one.**

Ship the loop. Polish later.

---

## 1. What the physical cell is

A two-robot semiconductor wafer-handling cell, physically built and partially
commissioned in the lab. The automated sequence is:

```
Wafer stand  →  [Dobot M1 Pro SCARA picks]  →  places on holder on conveyor
             →  [belt conveyor travels]      →  far end
             →  [myCobot Pro 600 unloads]    →  done
```

Sensors, PLC, and pneumatics tie the whole sequence together.

### Hardware inventory (confirmed from lab photographs, 2026-08-26 / 08-29)

| Item | Details |
|---|---|
| **Dobot M1 Pro** | SCARA arm. Mounted on black pedestal base, bolted to wooden board at one end of bench. Blue/white livery, "M1 Pro" badging. |
| **myCobot Pro 600** | Elephant Robotics, **6 DoF**, AC100-240V 50/60Hz. Confirmed from product label. Mounted on black base plate on wooden board at opposite end. |
| **Pro 600 controller** | Base unit exposes: Power Switch, Ethernet1, Ethernet2, USB1, USB2, Encoder (DB-style) port, 24V I/O terminal blocks. |
| **Belt conveyor** | Black belt, aluminium extrusion frame, ~60–70 cm long, motor at one end. Sits on bench between the two arms. |
| **Wafer** | Grey circular disc (silicon wafer). Observed resting on a **magenta/red 3D-printed holder block** on the conveyor belt. |
| **Wafer holders / nests** | **Blue 3D-printed curved cradles** on the bench — staging stand / wafer nests. |
| **PLC** | **Allen-Bradley Micro850**, cat. no. `2080-LC50-24QBB`, EtherNet/IP. |
| **Pneumatics** | Aluminium panel with vacuum ejector/generator, solenoid valves, pressure regulator, digital pressure switch (SMC-style), 24V terminal board. |
| **"Magic Box"** | 24V I/O breakout board, screw terminals, numbered channels — bridges field devices to PLC. |
| **Manual control panel** | Output1 / Output2, Input1 / Input2 selectors, ON/OFF, indicator lamps. |
| **Safety** | Multiple E-stops (red mushroom on yellow) at both arm stations. |

