## 5. Model availability — the hard constraints

### Dobot M1 Pro — **no public ROS 2 URDF exists**
This is the single biggest known gap and was verified by search.

- `smhaller/dobot-m1` — has URDF + meshes, but is **ROS 1** (Melodic-era). Porting
  requires: `package.xml` → format 3, `catkin` → `ament_cmake`, strip
  `roslaunch` files, keep only `urdf/` + `meshes/`.
- `Dobot-Arm/dobot_atom_ros2` — is ROS 2, but targets the **MG400**, not M1 Pro.
  Its xacro may still be a useful structural reference.

**Adopted strategy: placeholder-first.** Build the M1 Pro from primitive geometry
(boxes + cylinders) with SCARA kinematics — **2 revolute + 1 prismatic + 1
revolute** — so the pipeline (spawn → controllers → joint motion) can be validated
*immediately*, before real meshes exist. Swap `<geometry><box/></geometry>` for
`<mesh filename=.../>` later.

> **⚠️ Every dimension in the placeholder model is a stand-in. Replace with real
> spec-sheet values before trusting any reach or kinematics numbers.**

### myCobot Pro 600 — partial support, no exact match
- **`elephantrobotics/mycobot_ros2` (official)** — branches are only `foxy`,
  `galactic`, `humble`. **No `jazzy` branch.**
- **`automaticaddison/mycobot_ros2`** — the practical choice for Jazzy. Has ROS 2
  Control + MoveIt 2 + Gazebo + RViz, and Elephant Robotics themselves published
  a Jazzy/Ubuntu 24.04 sorting-station tutorial built on it.
- **`ABDULRAHMAN-ALSAADI/mycobot_ros2`** — personal fork, myCobot 280 on Jazzy.

**Caveat:** all confirmed-Jazzy repos target the **myCobot 280**, not the Pro 600.
The Pro 600 gap exists on Humble too — switching to Jazzy did not create it.
Plan: take the 280/320 xacro as a structural template and adapt link lengths /
meshes to Pro 600 geometry.

**TODO on first clone:**
```bash
ls src/mycobot_ros2/*/urdf/     # find which model folders actually exist
